This covers the game's graphics, its story and writing, and its design documents:

  Graphics
    art/                          all pixel art: characters, creatures, the mascot, tiles, objects, battle
                                  effects, the Bitmap8 font, and their previews
    src/gen/  (except data.js)    the built forms of that art (generated from art/ by tools/)
    tools/creature_designs/       the creature designs, drawn as vector shapes in Python
    tools/fx_designs.py           the battle-effect designs, drawn the same way
    tools/build_parcel.py         the parcel design, drawn the same way

  Story and writing
    src/game/tales/               the story decks: structures, settings, genres, premises and lines
    src/game/text.js              the game's words: dialogue, signs, books, television and chatter
    src/game/roster.js            the creature roster: names, types, temperaments and descriptions

  Design documents
    docs/design/                  the creature roster and story design notes

  dist/procedural-adventures.html bundles all of the above together with the code. The parts of it that come from
  the files listed here are under this licence; the rest is code, under LICENSE.

Not covered:
  Everything else in the repository is code, dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (LICENSE). That
  includes the rigs and build scripts that draw and convert the art (tools/creature_rig.py, tools/fx_rig.py,
  tools/build_*.py and the rest of tools/), and the music composer (src/engine/audio.js), so the music the game
  composes is not covered by this licence either.
  The text of Jane Austen's Pride and Prejudice (1813), from which place names, characters and quotations are
  taken (src/gen/data.js, built by tools/build_data.py), is in the public domain.

The Bitmap8 font (art/font/) is by The Buffalo, New York Procedural Amusements Coding Society; see art/font/CREDITS.txt.
